        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "9d5dde3a-7b2f-5ae1-9731-49ed79f286a7",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Hans Fallada, John Buchan\n- Works: Everyone Dies Alone, Every Man Dies Alone\n- Roles: writer, novelist, historian, politician, Governor General of Canada\n- Places: Germany, Canada, West Germany, Scotland\n\nFacts:\n- John Buchan was born on 26 August 1875 and later became the 15th Governor General of Canada since Canadian Confederation.\n- Hans Fallada, born Rudolf Wilhelm Friedrich Ditzen, was born on 21 July 1893 and was a German writer of the first half of the 20th century.\n- John Buchan, 1st Baron Tweedsmuir, died on 11 February 1940 after a career as a Scottish novelist, historian, and Unionist politician.\n- Hans Fallada died on 5 February 1947.\n- Everyone Dies Alone is a German film that was produced and released in West Germany in 1975.\n- Everyone Dies Alone was adapted from the Hans Fallada novel Every Man Dies Alone and originally bore the German title Jeder stirbt für sich allein.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
